<title>JAPAN: Japan 2-year note auction lowest price at 99.90.</title>
<headline>Japan 2-year note auction lowest price at 99.90.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Ministry of Finance said its auction of 120 billion yen in two-year government notes on Friday produced the following results:</p>
<p>Lowest price	 99.90    Stop rate	   0.950 pct</p>
<p>Average price	99.96     Average yield     0.920 pct</p>
<p>Total bids	   234.6 billion yen</p>
<p>Accepted Bids	118.2 billion yen</p>
<p>Bid to cover ratio 1.98 times</p>
<p>Bids accepted at lowest price 72.4000 pct</p>
<p>Issue date    Oct 21, 1996   Maturity    Oct 20, 1998</p>
</text>
